WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
999: an emergency. A crime happening now or someone in immediate danger. Also for an ambulance or the fire service. 101: the police when it is not urgent (reporting something that already happened, giving information, asking). 111: urgent health problems that are not life-threatening.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:30.500
If you call 999 from a mobile and cannot speak without putting yourself in danger, stay on the line; when asked, press 55 so they know it is a real emergency.

3
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:44.200
Domestic abuse: National Domestic Abuse Helpline, 0808 2000 247, free and 24 hours a day. You can ask for an interpreter: say the name of your language in English («Spanish, please»).

4
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.800
Say it aloud: “Spanish, please. I need an interpreter.”.
